[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Conversation" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://game/dialogue/conversation.gd" id="1_convo"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_convo")
id = &"n4_edwin"
text = "# DRAFT
# Edwin at dusk, on the west walk (night 4, fog). He has seen the demon's face; the dusk scene has him whisper it, and
# that he'll tell after Matins. Here he's jumpy and won't say more: after Matins, he swears it. (He dies before Matins.
# Nothing here says so.) The lines work whether or not the whisper has come yet.
== start
(Edwin on the west walk, his book hugged to his chest. He jumps when you come out of the fog, then laughs too loudly.)
Edwin: Alric! Don't come up on a man like that. Not in this.
-> topics

== again
(Edwin hasn't moved. He's watching the fog at the end of the walk.)
Edwin: Still here? Good. Stay a bit.
-> topics

== topics
* [if not n4_edwin_afraid] What has frightened you, Edwin? -> afraid
* [if not n4_edwin_fast] How are you bearing the fast? -> fast
* [if not n4_edwin_psalm] What are you reading? -> psalm

== afraid [set n4_edwin_afraid]
(He looks over your shoulder into the fog before he answers.)
Edwin: Not here. Not now. After Matins, I swear it. I'll come to your gate and tell you everything.
Edwin: Somebody's always listening in this house, Alric. Even in the fog. Especially in the fog.
-> topics

== fast [set n4_edwin_fast]
-> fast_bread [if n3_edwin_bread]
-> fast_plain

== fast_bread
Edwin: I left my bread last night, like we said. And now there's none to leave. I'm so hungry I could eat my book.
-> topics

== fast_plain
Edwin: No supper! I'm so hungry I could eat my book. Psalms and all.
-> topics

== psalm [set n4_edwin_psalm]
Edwin: The same as ever. Psalm ninety, the one we sing at Compline. You shall not fear the terror of the night.
Edwin: I've said it a hundred times since None. It isn't working.
-> topics

== leave
Edwin: After Matins, Alric. At your gate. Don't forget.
"
